  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🏺 Pottery Business Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a potter, a ceramics brand or a clay studio, from Dressed to Kiln to The Old Forge Pottery."
    },
    "intro": "A good pottery business name is warm, handmade and short enough for a maker's stamp: a clay pun, a homely object, or a studio name for classes and pottery painting. Selling mugs at markets, opening a clay studio or running pottery painting parties? This **pottery business name generator** has ceramics names in seven styles, ready to check before you stamp your pots.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good pottery business names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Coil & Trouble Ceramics</strong>: a pun on coil pots and Macbeth's witches.</li><li><strong>Glaze Days Pottery</strong>: a cheerful pun that suits a studio.</li><li><strong>The Smiley Milk Jug</strong>: cute and homely.</li><li><strong>Plum & Slip</strong>: slip is liquid clay, so it's a potter's in-joke.</li><li><strong>Saggar</strong>: a saggar is a box that protects pots in the kiln: short and modern.</li><li><strong>The Old Coach House Pottery</strong>: a classic name tied to a building.</li><li><strong>Try the Wheel</strong>: a studio name that tells beginners what to do.</li><li><strong>Sarah & Kiln</strong>: your name and the potter's oven.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Clay words that make good names",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Kaolin</strong> is china clay, named after Gaoling, a hill in China where it was mined.</li><li><strong>Slip</strong> is clay thinned with water, used to join and decorate.</li><li><strong>Bisque</strong> is a first, unglazed firing.</li><li><strong>Wedging</strong> is kneading clay to push out air.</li><li><strong>Raku</strong> and <strong>pit firing</strong> are firing methods that leave dramatic marks.</li></ul><p>The <strong>Studio</strong> style suits classes and pottery painting, where the name should sound fun and welcoming: <em>Messy Potters Club</em>, <em>Pot Shed Pottery Café</em>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
